WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.167 --> 00:00:02.602
-I had a big weekend
this weekend.

00:00:02.602 --> 00:00:03.936
-What did you do?

00:00:03.936 --> 00:00:05.538
-Well, I saw you for one of the
days, but you know that.

00:00:05.538 --> 00:00:08.674
But I went to Los Angeles,
'cause we went to meet

00:00:08.674 --> 00:00:10.777
some editors
and some media and press,

00:00:10.777 --> 00:00:12.979
and talking about
our year of our shows.

00:00:12.979 --> 00:00:15.447
We had a great year.
It's our fifth anniversary.

00:00:15.447 --> 00:00:18.818
So we had our -- Thank you.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:18.818 --> 00:00:20.052
So we talked about that.

00:00:20.052 --> 00:00:22.588
We did that first show
we did in Central Park.

00:00:22.588 --> 00:00:23.656
That was big.
-Oh, that was great.

00:00:23.656 --> 00:00:25.692
-The first-ever
live show outdoors.

00:00:25.692 --> 00:00:27.593
But then the
fifth-anniversary show special

00:00:27.593 --> 00:00:28.961
that we had
Tina Fey and Ben Stiller.

00:00:28.961 --> 00:00:30.763
It was like a
behind-the-scenes of our show,

00:00:30.763 --> 00:00:31.831
but it was all scripted.

00:00:31.831 --> 00:00:32.932
If you haven't seen it,
it's funny.

00:00:32.932 --> 00:00:35.134
It's a tricky show,
but it was good.

00:00:35.134 --> 00:00:37.770
And we talked about, obviously,
the Puerto Rico show.

00:00:37.770 --> 00:00:38.871
We took our show down
to Puerto Rico,

00:00:38.871 --> 00:00:40.039
and it was great.

00:00:40.039 --> 00:00:42.242
And it was just --
It was really fun to --

00:00:42.242 --> 00:00:44.310
Time to time, I go out to L.A.
just to say "hi"

00:00:44.310 --> 00:00:45.478
to everybody out there.

00:00:45.478 --> 00:00:50.283
And we also did a Q&amp;A at
the Writers Guild Theater

00:00:50.283 --> 00:00:53.252
with Guy Raz, who is the host of
"How I Built This."

00:00:53.252 --> 00:00:55.388
If you don't know that podcast,

00:00:55.388 --> 00:00:56.856
that should be on
your list of podcasts.

00:00:56.856 --> 00:00:59.258
It is one of the best out there.
He is phenomenal.

00:00:59.258 --> 00:01:00.292
But he was so great.

00:01:00.292 --> 00:01:02.195
And I was talking to him
about L.A.

00:01:02.195 --> 00:01:04.663
and when I was out there,
'cause I was there for a while,

00:01:04.663 --> 00:01:06.699
doing stuff before I got "SNL,"

00:01:06.699 --> 00:01:08.568
just struggling,
like everyone does.

00:01:08.568 --> 00:01:10.703
But that was fun.
I got to see some old friends.

00:01:10.703 --> 00:01:13.939
And I got to see Tom Rowan,
who's my --

00:01:13.939 --> 00:01:15.742
This guy has been
my lawyer since

00:01:15.742 --> 00:01:17.443
I think before I got
"Saturday Night Live."

00:01:17.443 --> 00:01:19.345
It was like, "You need to
get one, you know,

00:01:19.345 --> 00:01:20.780
when you're doing a contract
or something."

00:01:20.780 --> 00:01:22.481
So, he's the best.

00:01:22.481 --> 00:01:25.451
I mean, I've had him for
23 years, 22 years.

00:01:25.451 --> 00:01:27.887
Anyways, I'm firing him today
because I've had --

00:01:27.887 --> 00:01:29.922
The more I think about it,
I've had enough, yeah.

00:01:29.922 --> 00:01:33.058
No. I'm fed up, yeah.

00:01:33.058 --> 00:01:34.193
But he's the best guy.

00:01:34.193 --> 00:01:35.627
I love him so much
and his wife, Marla.

00:01:35.627 --> 00:01:37.029
They were there
in the front row.

00:01:37.029 --> 00:01:38.397
And it reminded me of
this story.

00:01:38.397 --> 00:01:39.799
They had a dinner party
at their house.

00:01:39.799 --> 00:01:41.801
I used to have dinner with them
when I'd go out to L.A.

00:01:41.801 --> 00:01:43.569
And, so, he goes, "I've got to
have dinner for you.

00:01:43.569 --> 00:01:44.737
Come on over.

00:01:44.737 --> 00:01:50.076
I got Carol Burnett,
Bob Newhart, Don Rickles,

00:01:50.076 --> 00:01:52.578
Tim Conway will be
at dinner.

00:01:52.578 --> 00:01:54.813
Yeah. So, I go over to
the house, I open the door,

00:01:54.813 --> 00:01:56.082
and they're all there.

00:01:56.082 --> 00:01:57.716
And I'm like "Oh, my gosh."
It was, like, fantastic.

00:01:57.716 --> 00:01:59.319
I see -- He goes,
"This is Carol Burnett."

00:01:59.319 --> 00:02:00.353
I go, "Hey, Carol.
Nice to meet you."

00:02:00.353 --> 00:02:01.620
He goes, "This is Bob."

00:02:01.620 --> 00:02:02.722
I go, "Hey, Bob.
Nice to meet you."

00:02:02.722 --> 00:02:04.123
He goes, "This is Tim."

00:02:04.123 --> 00:02:05.991
And Tim Conway goes, "You got to
get me the hell out of here.

00:02:05.991 --> 00:02:07.626
I don't know these people.

00:02:07.626 --> 00:02:09.928
I don't know who
these people are."

00:02:09.928 --> 00:02:12.631
That was his opening line.
Yeah, It was great.

00:02:12.631 --> 00:02:13.900
So, I did that.

00:02:13.900 --> 00:02:16.202
And we talked about everything
we do on the show.

00:02:16.202 --> 00:02:18.504
And, again, thank you to you,
Higgins, and The Roots,

00:02:18.504 --> 00:02:20.406
and all of our crew and everyone
who works hard on the show.

00:02:20.406 --> 00:02:21.540
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:21.540 --> 00:02:23.108
It was fun to talk about.

00:02:23.108 --> 00:02:26.479
I'd never really talked
that much about the show.

00:02:26.479 --> 00:02:28.648
But then, after we
did all that --

00:02:28.648 --> 00:02:30.549
It was Friday and Saturday.

00:02:30.549 --> 00:02:32.418
And then I was
trying to fly back,

00:02:32.418 --> 00:02:36.422
because I was nice enough to be
asked by the writers

00:02:36.422 --> 00:02:38.524
to do a cameo on
"Saturday Night Live"

00:02:38.524 --> 00:02:39.759
this Saturday.

00:02:39.759 --> 00:02:41.694
So, I'm doing L.A.

00:02:41.694 --> 00:02:44.396
And my man, Adam Sandler, is
hosting the show.

00:02:44.396 --> 00:02:48.667
He's my hero, my idol.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:48.667 --> 00:02:52.972
Adam Sandler is the nicest guy.
I just love him so much.

00:02:52.972 --> 00:02:54.340
He's just a --
-Gentleman.

00:02:54.340 --> 00:02:56.809
-Great guy,
just loyal, good dad,

00:02:56.809 --> 00:02:58.377
and just funny and just awesome.

00:02:58.377 --> 00:02:59.611
I just love him so much.

00:02:59.611 --> 00:03:01.181
So, I heard he was hosting.
He's never hosted.

00:03:01.181 --> 00:03:02.715
-Mnh-mnh.
-I find that hard to believe.

00:03:02.715 --> 00:03:04.717
-He didn't want to.
-That's bizarre.

00:03:04.717 --> 00:03:07.554
-It's up to him.
No one said "no."

00:03:07.554 --> 00:03:08.921
-I guess.

00:03:08.921 --> 00:03:12.659
But, yeah, so, he had a crusher
of a show, I thought.

00:03:12.659 --> 00:03:13.893
It was so great.

00:03:13.893 --> 00:03:16.595
And he had --
Chris Rock was there,

00:03:16.595 --> 00:03:19.399
who is one of
the funniest human beings ever.

00:03:19.399 --> 00:03:23.869
Kristen Wiig, who is just on
a different planet.

00:03:23.869 --> 00:03:25.237
But I loved his monologue.
It was good.

00:03:25.237 --> 00:03:27.106
I loved -- There were so many
great sketches.

00:03:27.106 --> 00:03:30.442
"Opera Man."
Opera Man is Robert Smigel.

00:03:30.442 --> 00:03:31.577
-Come on.
-Right?

00:03:31.577 --> 00:03:33.579
-Smigel and then Herlihy
helped on that one.

00:03:33.579 --> 00:03:35.214
-Tim Herlihy was there.

00:03:35.214 --> 00:03:36.749
And then, so, my scene was --

00:03:36.749 --> 00:03:40.052
It was the
Sandler family reunion.

00:03:40.052 --> 00:03:42.522
So, they had all of
his family at the reunion,

00:03:42.522 --> 00:03:44.090
and everyone talks
like Adam Sandler.

00:03:44.090 --> 00:03:45.358
-Yeah.

00:03:45.358 --> 00:03:48.861
-But, like, the fake comedy
characters, like...

00:03:48.861 --> 00:03:52.965
So, I came in...

00:03:52.965 --> 00:03:56.769
So, I came in --
Everyone's like...

00:03:56.769 --> 00:03:58.137
"Oh, yeah!"

00:03:58.137 --> 00:04:03.976
So, I came in and I was talking
to Smigel and Herlihy

00:04:03.976 --> 00:04:05.078
before the show,
'cause I was like,

00:04:05.078 --> 00:04:06.679
"I want to make Adam laugh.

00:04:06.679 --> 00:04:08.214
I want to see if
I can break him."

00:04:08.214 --> 00:04:09.882
Because I didn't
get to go to rehearsal,

00:04:09.882 --> 00:04:12.217
but I just landed just in time,
came right from the airport.

00:04:12.217 --> 00:04:15.421
I, like, smelled like airplane.
I'm like, "I can't wait.

00:04:15.421 --> 00:04:16.955
I'm so excited about this."

00:04:16.955 --> 00:04:19.792
I ran. I didn't run,
but I ran to my car.

00:04:19.792 --> 00:04:21.694
-Well, you ran to your car.
-Yeah, yeah.

00:04:21.694 --> 00:04:24.464
But then -- So, I got out there
and I didn't even know

00:04:24.464 --> 00:04:25.931
where to stand,
because I didn't rehearse.

00:04:25.931 --> 00:04:28.401
So I just assumed
I stand next to Sandler.

00:04:28.401 --> 00:04:29.435
And the cue cards are there.

00:04:29.435 --> 00:04:30.603
You know, I'm looking at that.

00:04:30.603 --> 00:04:36.376
So, I came out
and I read the lines like...

00:04:36.376 --> 00:04:38.110
And then I figured
I could make him laugh,

00:04:38.110 --> 00:04:41.547
because I can do like...

00:04:41.547 --> 00:04:44.450
That's a deep cut.
He doesn't do that anymore.

00:04:44.450 --> 00:04:46.852
You got to just...

00:04:46.852 --> 00:04:49.956
So, he started laughing
a little bit.

00:04:49.956 --> 00:04:53.759
So, anyways,
I'm usually in black ink

00:04:53.759 --> 00:04:55.594
on the cue cards from our show.

00:04:55.594 --> 00:04:58.330
But I forgot, I'm not the host.
-Yeah.

00:04:58.330 --> 00:05:00.033
-So, the host is in black ink.
-Black, yeah.

00:05:00.033 --> 00:05:02.201
-So I'm kind of
stalling for Sandler

00:05:02.201 --> 00:05:04.036
because I thought he
forgot his line.

00:05:04.036 --> 00:05:05.905
So I'm going like...

00:05:10.309 --> 00:05:11.577
And I'm looking at the cue card.

00:05:11.577 --> 00:05:12.945
And I don't know why
we even have cue cards.

00:05:12.945 --> 00:05:15.748
It was like,
"Hibbidy-hobbidy, yaba-haba."

00:05:15.748 --> 00:05:17.016
I don't remember if I said,

00:05:17.016 --> 00:05:19.619
"Yabbidy-hibbidy"
or "Hibbidy-yabbidy."

00:05:19.619 --> 00:05:21.187
I'm like,
"I don't know what to do."

00:05:21.187 --> 00:05:23.055
Anyways, I got
to, finally, my line.

00:05:23.055 --> 00:05:24.156
We did that.

00:05:24.156 --> 00:05:26.426
And it was just an honor
to do it with him,

00:05:26.426 --> 00:05:27.993
right in front of him,
'cause it's just --

00:05:27.993 --> 00:05:29.795
And he's just such a good dude.

00:05:29.795 --> 00:05:31.931
And he was so happy,
like, that night.

00:05:31.931 --> 00:05:35.867
And his wife, Jackie,
and two kids were there,

00:05:35.867 --> 00:05:36.969
and they're beautiful.

00:05:36.969 --> 00:05:38.170
I love those kids.

00:05:38.170 --> 00:05:39.905
And it was just --
Anyways, it was good.

00:05:39.905 --> 00:05:41.007
And then, at the end
of the night,

00:05:41.007 --> 00:05:43.609
he did this tribute to
Chris Farley.

00:05:43.609 --> 00:05:44.643
-Yeah.

00:05:44.643 --> 00:05:46.878
-And if you get a chance
to go online,

00:05:46.878 --> 00:05:49.749
it was so beautiful and so --
It was so funny, too.

00:05:49.749 --> 00:05:51.451
But I had heard all
the stories about Farley,

00:05:51.451 --> 00:05:53.619
and I just -- I wish I knew him.

00:05:53.619 --> 00:05:55.321
I got to meet him once,
but I just --

00:05:55.321 --> 00:05:57.523
He was singing this song,
and it's great,

00:05:57.523 --> 00:05:59.491
but it's also
a really nice tribute.

00:05:59.491 --> 00:06:02.028
And everyone was
just crying backstage.

00:06:02.028 --> 00:06:03.463
And it was just really touching.

00:06:03.463 --> 00:06:07.032
I mean, not just the audience,
but everybody that worked there,

00:06:07.032 --> 00:06:08.701
'cause the crew -- Some of
the crew -- they knew Farley.

00:06:08.701 --> 00:06:09.969
-Yeah.

00:06:09.969 --> 00:06:12.271
-So -- And I was next to Rock,
and it was just --

00:06:12.271 --> 00:06:13.372
It was really emotional.

00:06:13.372 --> 00:06:15.073
And I saw Smigel afterwards,

00:06:15.073 --> 00:06:16.909
and, usually,
he's always joking around.

00:06:16.909 --> 00:06:19.144
You know, he's like --
You know...whatever.

00:06:19.144 --> 00:06:21.680
So, I saw him, and he goes,
"Hey, man, that was great."

00:06:21.680 --> 00:06:23.449
And he's like -- I go,
"That was so touching."

00:06:23.449 --> 00:06:25.485
He goes --
He was behind the cast,

00:06:25.485 --> 00:06:28.487
and the cast were all kind of
hugging each other, crying,

00:06:28.487 --> 00:06:29.956
going like,
"Yeah, we're like family."

00:06:29.956 --> 00:06:31.423
It's like, you don't realize
it when you're there

00:06:31.423 --> 00:06:34.426
on "Saturday Night Live" for
whatever seasons you are there.

00:06:34.426 --> 00:06:36.161
You don't know when
some cast members

00:06:36.161 --> 00:06:37.763
are gonna go off
to do movies or --

00:06:37.763 --> 00:06:40.299
But that little moment of time,
that window of time,

00:06:40.299 --> 00:06:42.868
you hang out more
than your family.

00:06:42.868 --> 00:06:45.270
You really live with each other
and you don't realize it

00:06:45.270 --> 00:06:46.738
until, I think,
you get older and you go back

00:06:46.738 --> 00:06:48.140
and you go, "Oh, my gosh."

00:06:48.140 --> 00:06:50.776
And, so, he got me
filling up, Smigel.

00:06:50.776 --> 00:06:52.244
So I started crying
a little bit.

00:06:52.244 --> 00:06:53.346
I came up to your office
to see if you wanted

00:06:53.346 --> 00:06:54.479
to ride over to
the party together.

00:06:54.479 --> 00:06:57.950
-I was already drunk.

00:06:57.950 --> 00:06:59.351
-You don't even remember me

00:06:59.351 --> 00:07:00.452
coming and saying
"hello" to you.

00:07:00.452 --> 00:07:03.723
-You were there?
-I put smelling salts.

00:07:03.723 --> 00:07:05.124
I was there?

00:07:05.124 --> 00:07:09.161
And as I was going up, I got an
e-mail from Horatio Sanz,

00:07:09.161 --> 00:07:10.529
who is in L.A.

00:07:10.529 --> 00:07:11.964
And he was like, "Dude,
I'm watching the Sandler show

00:07:11.964 --> 00:07:15.300
right now and I'm just getting
sentimental, just missing us

00:07:15.300 --> 00:07:16.869
and missing -- You know.

00:07:16.869 --> 00:07:17.904
And I go, "wait until
you see the end."

00:07:17.904 --> 00:07:18.971
-Yeah.

00:07:18.971 --> 00:07:20.539
-I go, "You're gonna see
this Farley thing

00:07:20.539 --> 00:07:22.407
and you're just gonna lose it.

00:07:22.407 --> 00:07:23.776
This is like
when the show first started.

00:07:23.776 --> 00:07:25.144
But, anyways, it was just
kind of interesting

00:07:25.144 --> 00:07:26.545
that I got a thing from Horatio.

00:07:26.545 --> 00:07:27.746
I feel like I vibed him,

00:07:27.746 --> 00:07:29.715
'cause me and Horatio
were office-mates and

00:07:29.715 --> 00:07:31.183
comedy partners for years.

00:07:31.183 --> 00:07:34.620
I wouldn't be here
if it wasn't for Horatio.

00:07:34.620 --> 00:07:35.921
And, so, I got that.

00:07:35.921 --> 00:07:40.059
And then I thought it was the
best part was on Sunday.

00:07:40.059 --> 00:07:43.062
On Saturday night into Sunday,
it was trending all day,

00:07:43.062 --> 00:07:45.063
is Farley was trending.

00:07:45.063 --> 00:07:49.434
And I just thought, any kid that
was in mass or church Sunday

00:07:49.434 --> 00:07:53.072
and sneaking a look at Twitter
got to see Farley's name.

00:07:53.072 --> 00:07:55.641
And he would have
absolutely loved that,

00:07:55.641 --> 00:07:56.709
so I think that was a...

00:07:56.709 --> 00:07:59.412
[ Cheers and applause ]

